WEBVTT

00:09.564 --> 00:11.725
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar's instructions.

00:16.066 --> 00:24.368
[SPEAKER_00]: The foundation of these homoculae begin with a malleable clay, carefully sculpted into the likeness of small lizard-like creatures.

00:25.289 --> 00:27.269
[SPEAKER_00]: The choice of form is not arbitrary.

00:27.909 --> 00:32.631
[SPEAKER_00]: The lizard's form is simple and durable, unlike that of a spider or another insect.

00:33.513 --> 00:40.457
[SPEAKER_00]: Also with its ability to blend into surroundings, it is an ideal model for a creature designed for espionage.

00:41.317 --> 00:52.123
[SPEAKER_00]: The clay is imbued with a subtle enchantment by soaking it in warm water with one drop of its master's blood, making it receptive to the magical energies that will soon animate it.

00:53.583 --> 01:02.428
[SPEAKER_00]: The form can be as complex or as simple as desired, but a true artisan will ensure that the final form is both functional and aesthetically pleasing.

01:03.655 --> 01:19.656
[SPEAKER_00]: Central to the animation of Jody's homoculi are green gemstones, the ones gifted to me by the lithomancer Zafar Azane are similar to the stones used to create the animated blades that he is famous for.

01:21.108 --> 01:37.134
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar has informed me that he learned how to create these stones in the archives of the Arcane Order, a lost variation of a soul gem whose creation was discovered and perfected by the transmuters of the Suel Empire before the Twin Cataclysms.

01:38.235 --> 01:42.436
[SPEAKER_00]: One stone is known as the Heart Stone and is used to animate the homoculi.

01:43.016 --> 01:49.719
[SPEAKER_00]: The other is the Mind Stone, which the homoculi's master will use to animate the automaton itself.

01:50.997 --> 01:59.361
[SPEAKER_00]: Each gemstone is attuned to a specific frequency of arcane energy, a process that requires both skill and patience.

02:00.142 --> 02:10.487
[SPEAKER_00]: The heartstone is embedded within the clayform, nested where a heart might reside, and it is this stone that serves as the conduit for the master's will, via the mindstone.

02:12.776 --> 02:16.639
[SPEAKER_00]: The proper gemstone's ritual of animation is simple.

02:17.299 --> 02:25.244
[SPEAKER_00]: The master stands before the nascent homoculus, focusing his mind and channeling his thoughts through the mindstone.

02:26.165 --> 02:31.088
[SPEAKER_00]: The master intones the magical words, lapis philosophorum.

02:32.389 --> 02:38.693
[SPEAKER_00]: As the master's consciousness flows into the mindstone, the homoculus is awakened with the spark of life.

02:39.433 --> 02:41.575
[SPEAKER_00]: The connection is not one of domination.

02:42.388 --> 02:55.745
[SPEAKER_00]: But symbiosis, the homoculus becomes an extension of the master's mind, capable of executing complex tasks and relaying information with uncanny precision.

02:57.487 --> 03:00.772
[SPEAKER_00]: Once animated, the homoculi are remarkably resilient.

03:01.496 --> 03:09.222
[SPEAKER_00]: Unlike their traditional counterparts, they do not wither outside their jars or require a subsidence to survive.

03:09.863 --> 03:16.047
[SPEAKER_00]: Their clay bodies, reinforced by the magical properties of the Hearthstone, can withstand the rigors of their mission.

03:16.808 --> 03:27.836
[SPEAKER_00]: Should they sustain damage, a simple mending cantrip is sufficient to restore them to their original state, ensuring their longevity and continued service.

03:28.817 --> 03:36.879
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar informed me this implementation of Joe D's method of creating homoculi is but one of many possible paths to animation.

03:37.559 --> 03:50.982
[SPEAKER_00]: These homoculi, unlike their mythical phantoms, are not mere curiosities, but invaluable tools capable of performing feats that would be impossible for any ordinary spy.

03:51.622 --> 03:55.463
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly what I was hoping to be.

03:55.743 --> 03:57.563
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly why I wanted to wait.

03:59.318 --> 04:00.299
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

04:01.820 --> 04:03.722
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's cook one of those up.

04:03.902 --> 04:04.783
Okay.

04:05.443 --> 04:06.804
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you want to start that?

04:09.407 --> 04:11.648
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm hoping it's got some instructions, right?

04:12.469 --> 04:12.689
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

04:12.809 --> 04:13.610
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, absolutely.

04:13.650 --> 04:14.010
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

04:14.050 --> 04:16.392
[SPEAKER_00]: So, do you want to... You have the two stones.

04:16.573 --> 04:17.593
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I have the two stones.

04:17.694 --> 04:17.934
[SPEAKER_00]: Right?

04:18.234 --> 04:22.718
